From: corruptmods <13516012+corruptmods@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sd_ass: --sub-ass-render-threads

0205 calls ass_set_threads(renderer, 0) for every renderer, so libass
renders each frame with as many threads as there are logical cores, through
the threaded renderer of libass patch 0003, with no way for an embedder to
rule that path out or keep subtitle rendering off other cores.

--sub-ass-render-threads=<auto|1-64> is what get_renderer() passes; auto is
0, so the default is 0205's behaviour. 1 renders on the calling thread
only. A change reinitializes the subtitle decoder (UPDATE_SUB_HARD), so it
reaches the renderers it creates.

scripts/test_sub_ass_render_threads.sh compiles get_renderer() against
fakes and checks the value libass gets for the default, 1 and 4, and the
option's table entry.


diff --git a/DOCS/man/options.rst b/DOCS/man/options.rst
index 2d00dc6..c39ab4f 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/options.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/options.rst
@@ -2724,6 +2724,16 @@ Subtitles
 
     Default: 4 on Android, 0 elsewhere.
 
+``--sub-ass-render-threads=<auto|1-64>``
+    How many threads libass renders one subtitle frame with (per-event
+    threaded rendering, from the patched libass every build uses). ``auto``
+    uses every logical core; ``1`` renders on the calling thread alone, for
+    an embedder that wants to rule the threaded path out or keep subtitle
+    rendering off other cores. A change applies to the subtitle track's next
+    reinit.
+
+    Default: auto.
+
 ``--sub-ass-styles=<filename>``
     Load all SSA/ASS styles found in the specified file and use them for
     rendering text subtitles. The syntax of the file is exactly like the ``[V4
diff --git a/options/options.c b/options/options.c
index 1790c82..1fbd3e2 100644
--- a/options/options.c
+++ b/options/options.c
@@ -351,6 +351,9 @@ const struct m_sub_options mp_subtitle_sub_opts = {
         {"sub-ass-atlas-reuse", OPT_BOOL(sub_ass_atlas_reuse)},
         {"sub-ass-atlas-pool", OPT_INT(sub_ass_atlas_pool),
             M_RANGE(0, 8)}, // MP_ASS_PACKER_POOL_MAX
+        // ass_set_threads(): 0 (auto) is every logical core, as 0205 set it.
+        {"sub-ass-render-threads", OPT_CHOICE(sub_ass_render_threads, {"auto", 0}),
+            M_RANGE(1, 64), .flags = UPDATE_SUB_HARD},
         {0}
     },
     .size = sizeof(OPT_BASE_STRUCT),
diff --git a/options/options.h b/options/options.h
index 62ddc3d..eb5be63 100644
--- a/options/options.h
+++ b/options/options.h
@@ -136,6 +136,7 @@ struct mp_subtitle_opts {
     int sub_bitmap_max_size;
     bool sub_ass_atlas_reuse;
     int sub_ass_atlas_pool;
+    int sub_ass_render_threads;
     char **sub_avopts;
 };
 
diff --git a/sub/sd_ass.c b/sub/sd_ass.c
index e16ab9d..f47a0a1 100644
--- a/sub/sd_ass.c
+++ b/sub/sd_ass.c
@@ -298,7 +298,9 @@ static struct ass_render_state *get_renderer(struct sd *sd, int index)
         talloc_free(r);
         return NULL;
     }
-    unsigned threads = ass_set_threads(r->renderer, 0);
+    // --sub-ass-render-threads: 0 (auto) lets libass use every logical core.
+    unsigned threads = ass_set_threads(r->renderer,
+                                       MPMAX(sd->opts->sub_ass_render_threads, 0));
     if (threads)
         MP_VERBOSE(sd, "libass rendering threads: %u\n", threads);
     else
